d carrot is as much a straw hat right  now as vivi is but this number could  be intentionally misleading and might  refer to kinemon momo and a bunch of the  other samurai that supported this cause  additionally i'm interested in why she's  referring to them as  quote the moon obviously it works pretty  effectively for the analogy she's using  but  later in the next chapter it's revealed  that those supporting momonosuke's  efforts have tattooed a moon  onto their bodies also the verb that's  used in this  is woven now the only reference to  weaving anything in this story so far  has been this abandoned village at the  start of the act that ultima is from  where she would spend  all her days weaving hats now maybe that  location has some significance i mean  oda must have shown it to us for some  reason  there might be more to this but for now  i am reserving any further theories  because  what kinemon reveals later on is bloody  insane  this rocked my ever loving world  kinemon momonosuke and all the other  samurai that we've gathered over the  course of the last few hundred chapters  are all from 20 years in the past there  is no  time travel in one piece specifically as  kinemon recounts the events of kaido's  takeover 20 years ago describing the  events surrounding the death of lord  odin and the subsequent death of his  wife lady kuzuki toki  whom while holding her two children  momonosuke and his sister kiori  informs her loyal followers of the  following mankind cannot return to the  past  but it can leap into the future i have  used this strange time time ability to  travel further and further into the  future  until at last i arrive here at my final  destination  these quotes are ridiculously  interesting to me first of all it's  curious that she herself doesn't travel  forward in time with them it's implied  through kinemon's point of view that she  appeared to be someone that came from an  era long long ago yet despite having her  power to push people forward further  into time  she elects to stay behind and what's  more is this  she gives them momonosuke but not his  sister  that they've mentioned by name like four  panels ago personally i think this  sister  needs to play a big role in the story i  mean if she's inconsequential to the  story then they wouldn't have her as a  character in the first place  let alone a named character something  perhaps a little more minor is that she  refers to her power as  strange time time abilities instead of a  devil fruit power does she come from a  time where these powers weren't acquired  in the same way that they are now i've  got so many questions from this very  small but super interesting flashback  sequence  kinemon then goes on to describe how  they were thrust 20 years into the  future with their headstones visible and  their homeland in ruin he runs through  the series of events that led him to zou  dressrosa and eventually punk hazard  where they ultimately met in the first  place we learn that there's a sizable  following still in oneo that desires for  an uprising and thus they iron out a  plan  to raid kaido's base two weeks from now  on the night of the fire festival this  chapter  was exceptionally exposition heavy but  gave me  more than enough to think about when it  came to this world and what the  implications of it  might be now i'm exceptionally  interested in seeing how all of this  manifests later on  and now with kaido's name being thrown  around as a target and with how our  introduction to him a while back was  made i am intimidated by him but  also can't wait to see what he's made of  when luffy eventually clashes with him  down the road  chapters 921 922 and 923  alright so for those of you that haven't  seen this material before and are  currently thinking that everything up  until now in act one has been great  oh my sweet summer children y'all ain't  seen nothing yet because this next  section is the single most excited i've  been  while reading the entire story 900  chapters  this is the most excited i've been in  the entire story and that  includes marine ford  so kinemon runs through the current plan  trying to rally up the existing support  within the country to bolster the raid  makes sense and that's when we cut back  to the village all the food was given to  this thief with five a's in his name  atamayama  mole design up and boom jack is right  there looking for luffy but before they  can exchange even three sentences  this random thief it turns out he's a  samurai and an  awesome one at that slicing right  through jack with what looks like  relative ease so in my head i'm  wondering  okay so we're in act one and jack has  already been dealt with with  relative competence by a complete  unknown  yeah and then kaido shows up  and he's a massive freaking dragon i  swear mentally i was preparing myself  for jack  not kaido and certainly not super dragon  kaido the size of a town  it's an opponent with a presence size  and powers so far removed from anything  we've ever seen in the series including  big mom and whitebeard at least from a  visual level  it's also helped in large part because  at the beginning of the chapter things  were relatively calm they were  discussing things in secret and this  chapter ends with a giant kaido dragon  attacking a town what is happening  i don't know but what i do know is that  in the middle of law analyzing the  situation  luffy does say it with me now in typical  luffy fashion  runs off full speed ahead into the woods  towards kaido  the excitement i felt when reading this  was insane but seriously it only gets  better and  look i promise i'll analyze more towards  the end but god damn  this section got me so hyped it's unreal  so i got a vent  so as it happens kaido was drunk as all  hell and looking for some mighty brigand  he heard might have been the forest  at this time law catches up with luffy  during which time  hawkins catches up with kaido and in an  effort to divert his rampage away from  the village of bakuda  tells him that luffy and ko are at odin  castle ruins now what's important to  understand here is that he doesn't  actually know that they're there but  because  it's a legend that he believes will add  credibility to his claim for kaido  it just so happens that on that ruin are  in fact the straw hat pirates  and the rest of the remaining forces  hawkins is the best subordinate by the  way  so kaido just soars past luffy in the  blink of an eye before spitting fire  onto the ruins leveling the entire  area in a massive explosion luffy looks  on in utter disbelief and shock  faced with a similar reality he  experienced during the shabbat  archipelago arc  losing all of his friends in this moment  he shows a tremendous evolution of  character and strength of will as he  without delay  without crying deals an enormous  elephant gun straight to the head of  kaido and  at this moment i'm loving life so yeah  it's a pretty good chapter  crash landing onto the town below luffy  finds that something terrible has  happened to otama  at the hands of kaido as he made his way  to the village in the first place  enraged by this news luffy grits his  teeth punches the ground and screams  towards kaido  standing defiantly i'm right here kaido  in response  this asks who he is and without missing  a beat  cool as a cucumber the young man from  the east blue declares  kaido quickly unleashes a massive blast  from his mouth but by the time that  blast scorches the earth below  luffy is high in the air and begins  pummeling kaido with consecutive  colossal strikes  all over his body kaido falls to his  regular human form after this the crowd  remarks at what's happening to this god  among men  at the hands of a complete unknown luffy  engages gear 4 without delay and  unleashes everything he has successfully  meeting his mark  on the emperor of this  [Music]  the last chapter of act one after 923  chapters of emotional development  improvement and growth after mastering  his devil fruit power  upgrading it through the gears system  and after the leaps and bounds he's made  with hockey he unloaded it all on kaido  in a single chapter and with one blow  kaido knocks him out harder than any has  in the past without so much as a scratch  on him now that's an imposing villain  typically speaking this tactic for  establishing a villain or big bad by  donkey on the main characters super  early on  is a bit of a cliche but to be honest  it's not really a cliche or overdone at  all within one piece  and while this is the last chapter of  act one there's still some more  interesting and cool moments to speak of  on the cool front while luffy was  lying lifeless after the battle with  kaido and i use the word battle loosely  kaido remarks that luffy's been glaring  at him the entire time despite him  looking like he's not conscious at all  kaido walks off and that's when everyone  around luffy  falls to the ground while luffy was on  the verge of unconsciousness he  surprised kaido with his use of the  supreme king haki  i thought that was a pretty awesome  scene to be perfectly honest but in the  interest of wrapping things up the straw  hats on the hill were completely fine  because of the clutch use of a certain  female warrior's devil fruit power  frankie usop and robin hear that luffy  fought kaido and is being held prisoner  and they also make this face it's  wonderful  and when luffy's thrown into a cell he's  sharing it with  none other than kid another member of  the worst generation of pirates  what a crazy situation this should be  really interesting and with that the  curtain closes  on act 1. if i haven't made it  abundantly clear already  10 act 1 is phenomenal and easily my  favorite part of the post time skip  material it's stunningly beautiful  exceptionally well written and has a  super fun and straightforward story that  has hidden complexity  throughout for instance remember that  sword dealer way  back in low town that zoro gakitsu three  off  well during that chapter chapter 97  he said and i quote famous swordsmen  have died  tragic deaths because they wielded the  kitesu swords  this establishes the curse surrounding  the blades themselves obviously but  as we see earlier in this arc the  gentleman luffy yeets kittetsu  ii from refers to it as a cursed blade  yet again  now i'm not saying there's a correlation  between the sword and a curse  necessarily but  luffy and otama both met sinister ends  within this chapter  which is a wonderful bit of underlying  continuity i had to point out because it  was pointed out to me and i loved it  wano act one is most definitely  something i want to check out in the  anime in its  entirety after i catch up with the rest  of this series i cannot wait to see what  the rest of this amazing story will  continue to yield  as i venture into the second and third  acts in the coming weeks  if you would like to support this  channel on patreon you can do so for as  little as one dollar per video i've  uploaded all the videos in this series  that have been taken away by toei  so if you want to catch some of those  while i work out the illegal issues with  the evil japanese corporation you can do  so through the link in the description  but that'll do it for this video  as always i've been told not mark i'll  see you all next week and thank you so  much for watching
 

